<title>AUSTRALIA: Hardie sees A$10.5 mln loss from sale.</title>
<headline>Hardie sees A$10.5 mln loss from sale.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Building products group James Hardie Industries Ltd said on Wednesday that it would book a net loss of A$10.5 million on the sale of its 80 percent stake in private hospital operator Health Care Corp.</p>
<p>Alpha Healthcare Ltd said earlier that it would acquire the operation from James Hardie and Leighton Holdings Ltd for a total of A$38 million, to be funded by a mix of equity and debt.</p>
<p>James Hardie said the sale signalled its continuing disposal of non-core investments and its focus on fibre cement and related building products. -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
